345}, {"text": "In 79 AD, Mount Vesuvius had been dormant for centuries, so locals thought it was just a fertile mountain covered in vineyards.", "s": 5.525, "e": 15.498}, {"text": "When earthquakes rattled the city for days, residents assumed it was normal.", "s": 15.618, "e": 20.527}, {"text": "Then, at midday, Vesuvius erupted with 100,000 times the thermal energy of the Hiroshima bomb.", "s": 20.647, "e": 28.422}, {"text": "Within 24 hours, 20 feet of volcanic ash and pumice buried the city, freezing loaves of bread in ovens and preserving Roman daily life forever.", "s": 28.542, "e": 40.473}]}